/; FW_GC_STRESS
/; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
/; `spawn f()` queues a coroutine instead of calling it inline. The queued
/; coroutine runs once the main program body is done and the scheduler drains
/; its ready-queue, so "main done" must print BEFORE the coroutine's output.
/;
/; Under FW_GC_STRESS every allocation collects, so the string built inside
/; the spawned function must be rooted by that function's own shadow frame
/; while the scheduler is driving it — not just while `main` is on the stack.
/;
/; Arguments are deliberately absent here: passing them requires storing the
/; evaluated values somewhere GC-traced until the call actually happens. That
/; is a separate test once coroutines own a real stack.
/; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

fun greet() -> nthg {
  var msg: str = "hello " + "from-coroutine"
  println(msg)
}

spawn greet()
println("main done")
